    "id": 3943254722,
    "type": "DiffNote",
    "body": "[P2] Persist the bond together with freight acceptance\n\n**Location:** `src/vessels/vessels_contracts.c:555` (right, reviewed head `e2008096`).\n\nSave a captain with 1,000 gold, accept ten units of salt (a 140-gold bond), and crash before their next ordinary character save: the contract and ten cargo units are already in MySQL, but the player reloads with all 1,000 gold. `award_gold()` only changes the in-memory balance, and this acceptance path never calls `save_char_checked()`, so the newly introduced bond disappears while the freight remains deliverable or sellable. Conversely, `vessel_db_save_cargo()` silently returns on a write failure, so a later character save can retain the debit without durable freight. Make acceptance a checked, recoverable operation: persist the debit, transactionally update the contract and manifest, and roll back or reconcile all three records on failure before reporting success.\n\n**Validation:** Static tracing and a focused C control-flow probe using the unchanged acceptance function with stubbed game/database interfaces reproduced both outcomes. No full build, live server, or database integration suite was run.",
